{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfXzPjPAcYKZ2q5gH58wF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01R8wVYvbu2AG88hATLbg5AK","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\journal\\2026-09-29\\50-ship.md","content":"# Ship — 2026-09-29\n\n## @one-a-day/gaming/crossword-grid-card/v1 — Crossword Grid Card\n\nA still share card of a solved crossword, for the top of a blog write-up or a\nconstructor's new-puzzle post. It is for crossword bloggers (the Crossword\nFiend reviews open every post with a screenshot or phone photo of the app\nthey solved in) and for indie constructors who post a weekly `.puz`. The\ninputs are the puzzle file's own fields, given as props:\n\n- `grid`: the solution rows, \"/\" between rows, \"#\" or \".\" for a block;\n- `themeEntries`: clue ids such as \"17A 38A\";\n- `circles`: 0-based cell indices in the `.puz` order;\n- `title`, `author`, `publication`, `date`.\n\nThe card derives the clue numbers, tints the theme entries and lists their\nanswers, rings the circled squares, and writes the caption line\n(\"Demo Mini | Tue 9/29/26 | 7x7 | solution\"). `solved: false` gives the\nteaser: letters, tint and answers are hidden and nothing else moves. Square,\nlandscape and portrait canvases each get their own layout. Grids can be 3 to\n25 cells each way.\n\n## Render it\n\n```\nm0saic make @one-a-day/gaming/crossword-grid-card/v1 --template-repo . -w 1080 -h 1080 -o grid.png\n```\n\nProps worth trying (each one was rendered in this phase into\n[`ship/try/`](ship/try/). All exited 0 with no `[warn]`.):\n\n- the teaser: `--props '{\"solved\":false}'`\n- another highlighter: `--props '{\"themeColor\":\"#BDE3FF\"}'`. A fill under\n  4.5:1 against the ink is refused, and the error names the ratio.\n- a themeless Friday at link-share size:\n  `-w 1920 -h 1080 --props '{\"themeEntries\":\"\",\"circles\":\"\"}'`\n- a real-size 15x15: `--props @journal/2026-09-29/stress/15x15.props.json`\n  ([`ship/try/15x15-file.png`](ship/try/15x15-file.png))\n\nWhy it exists (the tutorial):\n\n```\nm0saic make @one-a-day/gaming/crossword-grid-card/v1 --template-repo . --tutorial -w 1280 -h 720 -o why.mp4\n```\n\n## What the ship phase did\n\n- The pick (a) was already in place, so no copy was needed.\n- The template's picture did not change. The three renders in\n  [`ship/renders/`](ship/renders/) are byte-identical to the\n  `variants/a/renders/` the critic judged, and the layout fingerprint is\n  unchanged. `variants/a/` is left as it was judged. The shipped state,\n  tutorial included, is in [`ship/`](ship/).\n- Changed, from the critique's polish list:\n  - Tutorial page 2 no longer says the `.puz` \"holds all of it\". It now\n    says the `.puz` holds the grid, title, author and circles, but not the\n    theme ([`ship/stills/tutorial-2.png`](ship/stills/tutorial-2.png)).\n  - Page 3 says \"two text sources, one holding every letter and one every\n    number\" instead of \"one text source for every letter\"\n    ([`tutorial-3.png`](ship/stills/tutorial-3.png)).\n  - `WHY.timeline` is the finished trace: all 7 phase calls, scout to\n    critique ([`tutorial-6.png`](ship/stills/tutorial-6.png)).\n  - The `title` and `date` descriptions shown in Make read \"Puzzle title\" and\n    \"Puzzle date\", not \"CrosswordPuzzle ...\".\n- Checks, in the order the task gives them:\n  - `npm run build`, `npm run previews` (1 minted), `npm run build`,\n    `npm run fingerprints:update` (12 unchanged), then `npm run verify`,\n    which exited 0: lint, 182 jest tests, 54 pipeline tests, the contract\n    and deps ([`logs/ship-verify.log`](logs/ship-verify.log)).\n  - `m0saic doctor . --json` (0.3.0) returned `\"ok\": true` with 0 errors and\n    0 warnings for this template\n    ([`logs/doctor-ship.json`](logs/doctor-ship.json)). Its 4 warnings and\n    the \"lagging\" entries belong to frozen templates.\n  - `--validate-only` and `--tutorial --validate-only` both exited 0.\n  - `check-why` was clean.\n- Preview: [`preview.png`](../../assets/templates/@one-a-day__gaming__crossword-grid-card__v1/preview.png)\n  is 1920x1080 and 162 KB, the landscape card at its defaults. It is the\n  same bytes as `variants/a/renders/landscape.png`. This is an image\n  template, so there is no first frame to go blank.\n\n## Weak spots (honest; a human polish pass starts here)\n\n- **There is no `.puz`/`.ipuz` parser.** A blogger has to get the solution\n  string out of the file (puzpy's `p.solution`) or retype the rows. They also\n  type the theme ids and the circle indices by hand, and 0-based row-major\n  indices are tedious to count. An unbroken solution string only works for a\n  square grid. This is the main reason the critic gave the brief's\n  usefulness line a 1: a screenshot still takes seconds.\n- **The theme list shrinks at Sunday size.** On a 21x21 with 8 answers, the\n  answers sit at about 10 px under a 14 px heading\n  ([`stress/21x21-1080.png`](stress/21x21-1080.png)). In the square layout,\n  five or more answers switch to two sub-columns, and the size drops from\n  19 px to 10-13 px.\n- **The landscape card has empty space.** The browse card shows it: title at\n  the top, a two-line list in the middle and the caption at the bottom, with\n  about 320 px of nothing between them.\n- **The contract is partly hollow.** The `cell-letter` and `cell-number` fits\n  are measured against the whole board, so the build cannot catch a glyph\n  that outgrows its cell. Equal cells are asserted only in the test.\n- **The `date` handle sits on derived text** (\"| Tue 9/29/26\", not the\n  YYYY-MM-DD the prop holds).\n- **Not drawn:** rebus squares (only the first letter shows), shaded squares\n  and clue text.\n- **Small floors:** a 48-character author of wide letters drops the byline\n  to 7 px at 480x270. At 4:5 and 5:4, which are not contract canvases, the\n  portrait header runs 5 px into the gutter and the landscape board floats.\n- **A CLI wording issue, not a template one:** the too-dark `themeColor`\n  refusal reaches the user as \"Error running ffmpeg: ... themeColor #223355\n  is too dark ...\". The template's message is right, but the prefix\n  misleads.\n- **Two things about tutorial page 6:**\n  - \"build (4)\" is drawn red because the runner killed that call at its\n    timeout. The agent had finished at 11:34 (`END ok`, $31.73, per\n    [`logs/build-4.log`](logs/build-4.log)), but the process did not exit.\n  - The page's \"2h 34m wall time\" includes the 51 minutes between the\n    session-limit stop and the resume. This ship phase is not on the page,\n    because it is still running when the spec is written.\n\n## Follow-ups (what v2 would do)\n\n- A `.puz`/`.ipuz` to props converter, so the grid, title, author and\n  circles come from the file. That is what would make the card faster than\n  a screenshot for a blogger.\n- Pick the theme list's sub-column count by the text size it yields, or take\n  height from the board as the long title already does, with the heading's\n  size as the floor.\n- Check each glyph against one cell (`hole(0)`) in the layout contract, not\n  against the board band.\n- Fill the landscape panel: a larger list, or give the board more width when\n  the list is short.\n- Draw shaded squares (`.ipuz` carries them) and rebus cells. Make a video\n  teaser that fills the grid in.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":605,"cache_read_input_tokens":128322,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":605},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"af1c23bb-6b01-433b-b16a-de6cab8056e5","uuid":"1b72fec5-e316-472d-8086-0ee49d0ebc63","timestamp":"2026-09