{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfXzSZ4syRz6UZ4SLvA87","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0174E2YcayJ72TAo7SVRypmU","name":"Workflow","input":{"script":"export const meta = {\n  name: 'ship-verify-2026-09-29',\n  description: 'Adversarially verify the ship note, the edited why-tutorial and gate readiness (read-only)',\n  phases: [\n    { title: 'Review', detail: 'three lenses: ship-note facts, tutorial truth, gate readiness' },\n    { title: 'Verify', detail: 'a skeptic per lens tries to refute each finding' },\n  ],\n}\n\nconst REPO = 'C:\\\\src\\\\m0saic-production\\\\one-a-day'\nconst COMMON = `You are checking the SHIP phase of the one-a-day run for 2026-09-29 in the repo at ${REPO} (Windows; the Bash tool is Git Bash). The template is @one-a-day/gaming/crossword-grid-card/v1 at src/gaming/crossword-grid-card/v1/. Today's journal is journal/2026-09-29/ (state.json, run.json, 10-scout.md, 20-brief.md, 30-build.md, 40-critique.md, 50-ship.md, variants/a|b|c/, ship/, stress/, logs/).\n\nSTRICTLY READ-ONLY. Do NOT edit, write, move or delete any file. Do NOT run npm run build / npm test / npm run verify / npm run previews / fingerprints:update / render-variant / m0saic make (they rewrite dist/, renders or the manifest and another process owns the tree). You MAY run: cat/sed/grep/ls/cmp/sha256sum, node -e scripts that only READ files, git status/diff/log (never commit/checkout/reset), 'm0saic doctor . --json' is NOT allowed either (it is slow and already logged in journal/2026-09-29/logs/doctor-ship.json). You may use WebFetch for public facts about the .puz / .ipuz formats or puzpy.\n\nReport only REAL defects: a claim that is false or unsupported by the files, a wrong number, a broken relative link, a rule the gate or AGENTS.md would refuse. Style nits are not findings. For each finding give the exact file and the evidence (the command you ran and what it printed, or the line you read). If everything checks out, return an empty findings list.`\n\nconst FINDINGS = {\n  type: 'object',\n  properties: {\n    findings: {\n      type: 'array',\n      items: {\n        type: 'object',\n        properties: {\n          file: { type: 'string' },\n          claim: { type: 'string', description: 'the exact text or behaviour that is wrong' },\n          severity: { type: 'string', enum: ['high', 'medium', 'low'] },\n          evidence: { type: 'string' },\n          fix: { type: 'string', description: 'the smallest correct wording or change' },\n        },\n        required: ['file', 'claim', 'severity', 'evidence', 'fix'],\n      },\n    },\n    checked: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' }, description: 'claims or checks you verified as TRUE (short)' },\n  },\n  required: ['findings', 'checked'],\n}\n\nconst VERDICTS = {\n  type: 'object',\n  properties: {\n    verdicts: {\n      type: 'array',\n      items: {\n        type: 'object',\n        properties: {\n          claim: { type: 'string' },\n          refuted: { type: 'boolean', description: 'true if the finding is NOT a real defect' },\n          reason: { type: 'string' },\n          fix: { type: 'string', description: 'if real: the corrected wording/change you would apply' },\n        },\n        required: ['claim', 'refuted', 'reason', 'fix'],\n      },\n    },\n  },\n  required: ['verdicts'],\n}\n\nconst LENSES = [\n  {\n    key: 'ship-note-facts',\n    prompt: `${COMMON}\n\nLENS: fact-check journal/2026-09-29/50-ship.md line by line. For every factual statement (numbers, file names, byte sizes, \"byte-identical\", exit codes, test counts, pixel sizes, the critic's scores, the build-4 timeout story, the 51-minute gap, the \"2h 34m\", the stress numbers, each relative markdown link resolving to an existing file from journal/2026-09-29/), find the file that proves or disproves it. Sources of truth: logs/ship-verify.log, logs/doctor-ship.json, logs/ship-render.log, logs/ship-tutorial-validate.log, logs/ship-validate.log, logs/build-4.log, trace.json (node pipeline/lib/trace.mjs --timeline journal/2026-09-29/trace.json prints the timeline), 30-build.md, 40-critique.md, ship/report.json, ship/try/*.log, variants/a/renders/, assets/templates/@one-a-day__gaming__crossword-grid-card__v1/preview.png. Also check the file follows the required skeleton: '# Ship — 2026-09-29', '## @one-a-day/<pack>/<slug>/v1 — <Title>' with one descriptive paragraph, '## Render it' with the render one-liner, props worth trying and the tutorial one-liner, '## Weak spots (honest; a human polish pass starts here)', '## Follow-ups (what v2 would do)'. Extra sections are allowed.`,\n  },\n  {\n    key: 'tutorial-truth',\n    prompt: `${COMMON}\n\nLENS: is the edited why-tutorial TRUE? Read the WHY literal in src/gaming/crossword-grid-card/v1/crossword-grid-card.ts (problem, solution, caveats, usage, timeline) and the rest of that file. Check in particular: (1) problem[1] now says \"The .puz on the same site holds the grid, title, author and circles, but not the theme.\" - is that accurate for the Across Lite .puz format (solution grid, title, author, copyright, clues, notes; GEXT extension for circled squares) and does the scout (10-scout.md) support that the .puz is offered on the same site (crosswordfiend.com/download/)? Is \"not the theme\" fair (the theme ids the card needs are not a .puz field)? (2) solution[1] says the board is \"a few masked layers (paper, theme tint, ink with the paper cells cut out, rings) plus two text sources, one holding every letter and one every number, on one integer lattice. A 25x25 takes no more layers than a 7x7 (8 at most)\" - count the board layers drawCrosswordCard actually adds and check the claim. (3) caveats and usage.try against the code (parseCrosswordGrid, normalizeCrossword) - e.g. the square-only unbroken string, the 6 px number floor, rebus first letter. (4) timeline equals the output of 'node pipeline/lib/trace.mjs --timeline journal/2026-09-29/trace.json' exactly. (5) dist/gaming/crossword-grid-card/v1/crossword-grid-card.js contains the same edited WHY text (i.e. dist was rebuilt after the edit). (6) the rendered pages journal/2026-09-29/ship/stills/tutorial-2.png, tutorial-3.png, tutorial-6.png show the new wording (view them with the Read tool). Also flag any remaining sentence in the WHY that overclaims a feature the code lacks.`,\n  },\n  {\n    key: 'gate-readiness',\n    prompt: `${COMMON}\n\nLENS: would the runner's gate (pipeline/lib/gate.mjs - read it) ship this day, and are the phase's hard rules kept? Check: (a) git status: only allowed paths changed (node --input-type=module -e \"import {classifyChanges,porcelain} from './pipeline/lib/git.mjs'; console.log(JSON.stringify(classifyChanges(porcelain('.'),{date:'2026-09-29'}),null,1))\" from the repo root - report forbidden/scratch entries and newTemplateDirs); nothing under pipeline/, tools/, AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, README.md, .github/, package.json, dep-allowlist.json, frozen.manifest.json or another day's journal changed; no stray out.*/why.*/*.validate.json/*.output.json at the repo root. (b) exactly one new template folder; no frozen template (listed in frozen.manifest.json) modified (node tools/check-freeze.mjs is read-only - you may run it). (c) state.json has decision \"ship\", pick \"a\", critique \"done\" and does NOT yet have ship \"done\" (that is set last, by the caller); run.json model.selfDeclared is set and model.corrected untouched (null). (d) template-manifest.json has the template with its preview image path and the file exists and is > 5 KB. (e) logs/doctor-ship.json ok:true and no error whose templateId is this template; logs/ship-verify.log shows verify succeeded (lint, jest, pipeline tests, contract, deps). (f) src/gaming/crossword-grid-card/v1/*.ts contain no Math.random, Date.now, new Date(, process.env, fetch(, or non-ASCII characters in rendered copy (the label's ' · ' middle dot in the label field is the scaffold's convention and is allowed). (g) dist/ is fresh relative to src (compare the WHY text or mtimes). (h) src/gaming/index.ts uses export * only. Report any condition that would fail the gate.`,\n  },\n]\n\nconst results = await pipeline(\n  LENSES,\n  (lens) => agent(lens.prompt, { label: `review:${lens.key}`, phase: 'Review', schema: FINDINGS }),\n  (review, lens) => {\n    if (!review) return { lens: lens.key, review: null, verdicts: [] }\n    if (!review.findings.length) return { lens: lens.key, review, verdicts: [] }\n    return agent(`${COMMON}\n\nYou are a SKEPTIC. Another reviewer (lens: ${lens.key}) reported the findings below. For EACH one, independently re-check the evidence in the files and try to REFUTE it: is the claimed defect real, or is the original text actually correct / the reviewer misread? Default to refuted=false only when you reproduced the defect yourself. For a real one, give the smallest correct fix.\n\nFINDINGS:\n${JSON.stringify(review.findings, null, 2)}`, { label: `verify:${lens.key}`, phase: 'Verify', schema: VERDICTS })\n      .then((v) => ({ lens: lens.key, review, verdicts: v ? v.verdicts : [] }))\n  },\n)\n\nreturn results.filter(Boolean)\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1371,"cache_read_input_tokens":132026,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1371},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"af1c23bb-6b01-433b-b16a-de6cab8056e5","uuid":"c3a7b3a7-406d-4f05-af38-b74e9be00ce7","timestamp":"2026-09-29T15:47:02.310Z","request_id":"req_011CfXzSYVfBnfZkvsU1nUwx","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_0174E2YcayJ72TAo7SVRypmU":{"script":"export const meta = {\n  name: 'ship-verify-2026-09-29',\n  description: 'Adversarially verify the ship