{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XqqAHoCKU4H8NVDS4q7o19","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n \"file\": \"src/gaming/crossword-grid-card/v1/crossword-grid-card.ts\",\n \"claim\": \"WHY.solution[1] (line 788): \\\"the board is a few masked layers (paper, theme tint, ink with the paper cells cut out, rings) plus two text sources ... A 25x25 takes no more layers than a 7x7 (8 at most)\\\". The \\\"8 at most\\\" is right, but the list is wrong. The paper layer has no mask, and the two masked number-knockout layers are left out. A reader who counts the list gets 4 + 2 = 6 and cannot see where 8 comes from.\",\n \"severity\": \"low\",\n \"evidence\": \"drawCrosswordCard line 674: `add(ink, 1, tag(makeColorTile(PAPER), \\\"board-paper\\\"))` has no mask. Lines 711-712 add masked PAPER and themeColor \\\"number-knockout\\\" layers (5, 6). I ran node on the built dist module with circles \\\"0 14 15 16 28 29 30\\\" and themeEntries \\\"1A\\\", on both the default 7x7 and a 25x25 at 1080x1080. Each printed `8 board-paper,theme-tint,board,rings,number-knockout,number-knockout,cell-number,cell-letter masked: theme-tint,board,rings,number-knockout,number-knockout`. So the maximum is 8 and it does not depend on grid size, which is true. But board-paper is not masked, and the knockouts are real layers the parenthesis does not name. The same text is on ship/stills/tutorial-3.png.\",\n \"fix\": \"Replace solution[1] with this (316 chars, under the 320 budget): \\\"The decision that matters: the board is a few layers (paper, theme tint, ink with the paper cells cut out, rings, knockouts) plus two text sources, one holding every letter and one every number, on one integer lattice. A 25x25 takes no more layers than a 7x7 (8 at most), and every size 3 to 25 renders the same way.\\\" Then rebuild and re-render the tutorial.\"\n}\nCHECKED: problem[1] .puz claim is accurate. puzpy FileFormat.md says: strings are title, author, copyright, clues, notes; the solution board uses '.' for blocks; GEXT is one byte per square with 0x80 = circled; there is no theme field. So \"holds the grid, title, author and circles, but not the theme\" is fair. The theme ids really are typed by hand in themeEntries. || The scout supports \"the .puz on the same site\". 10-scout.md quotes the Fiend download page (\"download today's puzzles in either AcrossLite (puz) or Adobe (pdf) format\"), and scout-1.jsonl logs that page as opened with that quote. WebFetch of crosswordfiend.com/download/ returned 403 today, so I could not re-check it live. || The problem[0] file names and the WSJ caption appear word for word in 10-scout.md. || Board layer count: drawCrosswordCard adds at most 8 board pieces (paper, tint, ink, rings, 2 knockouts, numbers, letters). That is the same for 7x7 and 25x25, confirmed by running the dist module. || Caveat 'Clue numbers are dropped below 6 px, so a 15x15 at 480x270 shows letters only' is true: pitch 16.47, numberPx round(4.61)=5 -> 0, letterPx 10. Board pieces are board-paper, board, cell-letter only. At 640x360 the numbers come back at 6 px. || Caveat 'Grids 3 to 25' matches MIN_SIDE=3, MAX_SIDE=25. A non-square unbroken string fails with 'must have 3-25 rows (got 1)', so 'paste a non-square grid as rows split by \"/\"' is correct. || Rebus caveat is true. FileFormat.md: 'only the first letter will be given by the solution board'. The parser accepts a single A-Z character per cell. || Shaded squares, clue text and animation are absent from the code, as the caveats say. solved=false hides letters, tint and the answer list (showThemes, themeCells and lets are all gated on p.solved). || usage.try: parseCrosswordGrid('PAN.BOWAGE.AREDOGSLED..AIL..CATNAPSOWE.SATYES.TRY') parses as 7x7. Circles '14 15 16' are white cells in the default grid. The themeEntries example '17A 38A 61A' is a format example: it would be refused against the default 7x7 (no 38A), but the line points to the reader's own write-up, so I did no