escription, which also went into the manifest. It now describes the card.\n\n**Review:** before marking the phase done, I ran three read-only reviewers, each followed by a skeptic trying to disprove its findings. Five findings held up and all are fixed:\n- the page 3 layer list;\n- the registry placeholder;\n- three mistakes in my draft of `50-ship.md`. I had the build-4 timeout backwards: the agent finished, then kept working after the runner's stop signal failed to end it. I also called 54 tests \"pipeline tests\" (44 are). And I misnamed the critic's rubric line.\n\nI rendered the shipped state into `journal/2026-09-29/ship/` and left `variants/a/` exactly as the critic judged it. The four \"props worth trying\" examples in `50-ship.md` each rendered without errors, into `ship/try/`.\n\n**Weak spots, all listed in `50-ship.md`:**\n- There is no `.puz` parser, so a blogger still retypes the grid, theme ids and circles. That is why the critic scored usefulness 1 of 2.\n- The theme list gets small on a Sunday-size 21x21 (answers about 10 px).\n- The landscape card has large empty gaps.\n- The layout check that letters fit their squares only runs in the test, not in the build.\n- Tutorial page 6 draws \"build (4)\" in red because the trace records that call as timed out. Its wall time also includes the 51-minute wait before the resume."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":202,"cache_read_input_tokens":166205,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":202},"output_tokens":695,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"af1c23bb-6b01-433b-b16a-de6cab8056e5","uuid":"27c20547-6abc-44ea-a38a-9e9e10aae73b","timestamp":"2026-09-29T16:00:06.361Z","request_id":"req_011CfY1Tw4rwUzATz8kHLJkf"}
